      "id": "mvp",
      "status": "implemented",
      "objective": "Keep the pinned portable Staging launcher and its domain boundaries safe while allowing one explicit single-PR maintenance contract to cover repository-side Production MCP/OAuth ingress hardening after the affected parallel workstreams are already integrated.",
      "e2e_journeys": [
        {
          "id": "external-ssd-and-mcp-ingress-maintenance-closure",
          "end_to_end": true,
          "level": "synthetic_runtime",
          "actor": "Platform maintainer",
          "entrypoint": "autopilot-portable-staging/Start-AutoPilot.ps1 and repository MCP/OAuth governance gates",
          "terminal_outcome": "The exact repository tree is accepted only when Staging remains isolated, Production MCP/OAuth metadata is fail-closed behind trusted ingress, host authority is shared, and the maintenance PR covers every changed runtime file without provider or secret mutation.",
          "steps": [
            "Require an exact 40-character commit SHA for portable Staging execution and reject dirty or non-local execution contexts before local mutation.",
            "Keep Production and Staging hostname families isolated while allowing only the declared Cloudflare/Hostinger DNS record-type set in repository policy.",
            "Require all three Production trusted-ingress declarations before OAuth metadata can be served under Production semantics.",
            "Resolve external host authority through one shared fail-closed resolver so caller-supplied forwarded-host values cannot select another public surface unless proxy-host trust is explicitly enabled.",
            "Keep Hostinger R7 readback GET-only while verifying runtime identity plus protected-resource and authorization-server metadata without provider mutation.",
            "Require the changed single-PR maintenance contract to declare secrets_included=false and cover every changed runtime file that overlaps already-integrated parallel feature contracts."
          ],
          "assertions": [
            "The exact Staging commit is pinned and read back before service startup.",
            "MIGRATION_APPLIED=false and DATABASE_MUTATED=false remain required and exact for portable Staging.",
            "Production hostnames never route to local Staging, and Staging hostnames never route to Hostinger Production.",
            "Production DNS policy requires proxied Hostinger routing and explicitly permits only A or CNAME record types without performing provider mutation.",
            "Production OAuth protected-resource and authorization-server metadata fail closed when trusted ingress is not fully attested.",
            "The shared trusted-host resolver ignores forwarded host headers unless REMOTE_MCP_TRUST_PROXY_HOST_HEADERS is exactly true and rejects malformed or multi-valued hosts.",
            "R7 remains GET-only and performs no POST, deployment, provider mutation, database mutation, migration, or secret payload access.",
            "The maintenance exception cannot activate unless one schema-valid single_pr contract declares secrets_included=false and covers all changed runtime files.",
            "The two Staging-only Act-as-User control routes are source-bound in the precise OpenAPI route-contract registry and canonical document while their schema keeps live_execution_allowed=false, write_activation_allowed=false, database_mutation_allowed=false, and secrets_included=false.",
            "No secrets are included in this E2E contract or its evidence."
          ],
          "tests": [
            {
              "id": "domain-family-policy-regression",
